  "published": "2026-10-28T12:11:18.723Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "#### Added\n- Multi-targets `net10.0` and `net11.0`; on `net11.0` the platform control adapters use the new .NET 11 `Process` APIs (`Process.Signal`, `TryWaitForExitStatus`, `TryGetProcessById`). Windows and macOS children start suspended and resume only after the configured `ProcessResourcePolicy` is applied.\n\n#### Changed\n- `CliInvoke` adopts `Squash` (2.1.0) build-time trimming. The IL linker now strips unreachable non-public code from the shipped assemblies at Release build time; the public API surface is untouched. Measured as of this release: CliInvoke.dll for net10.0 TFM shrinks ~37% (218 KB → 138 KB) and the package as a whole shrinks ~15% (311 KB → 264 KB) - the removed code is almost entirely unreferenced Polyfill-emitted types.\n- `Polyfill` bundling moved here from `CliInvoke.Core` (which is now dependency-free)\n- `CliRun.FireAndForget(ProcessConfiguration)` fails fast on redirected configurations (`ArgumentException` before start) - the handle is disposed immediately after launch, so redirected pipes would never be drained.\n- `ExternalProcess` resolves `TargetFilePath` once at construction; an unresolvable path now throws `FileNotFoundException` there instead of at start, and repeat starts reuse the resolved path.\n- Retry middleware rewinds seekable standard input (`Position = 0`) before every retry attempt; a non-seekable stdin source throws `InvalidOperationException` when a retry would occur.\n- `LoggingMiddleware` logs the joined `ArgumentList` when the argument string is empty.\n- Updated `Microsoft.Extensions.*` dependencies to 10.0.14.\n\n#### Fixed\n- Raw-mode invocations no longer deadlock on chatty children: `OutputRedirection` is forced off before start in `InvocationMode.Raw` (caller configuration untouched).\n- Buffered cancellation is deterministic: a drain-side `OperationCanceledException` is absorbed under `CancellationThrowsException=false` and propagated when `true`.\n- Wait paths poll for actual child exit after a forceful kill, so `ExitCode` is readable immediately after a kill-timed-out wait.\n- `AllowExceptionsIfUnexpected` no longer swallows genuine failures that resolve near an expected timeout - only CliInvoke's own cancellation `OperationCanceledException`s are absorbed.\n- Null environment-variable values reach the child process for removal instead of being dropped by the control adapter.\n- `ProcessResult.Signal` is correct on the `net11.0` Unix leg: raw native signal numbers are mapped through the platform table before the SIGKILL and unknown-signal filters.\n- `LoggingMiddleware` argument redaction works again (`RegexOptions.ExplicitCapture` had broken capture references, emitting the redaction marker with the wrong formatting).",
